13. Why -ExpandProperty Name?

Nice little PowerShell concept here.

Instead of storing the complete service objects and display formatting, the lab extracts the Name value.

So instead of lots of columns:

Status    Name            DisplayName...


you get essentially:

AarSvc
AJRouter
ALG
AppIDSvc
...


That makes comparison easier.

14. Services differential analysis

Current services:

$servicesnow = Get-Content .\services.txt


Baseline:

$servicesbaseline = Get-Content baseline\services.txt


Then:

Compare-Object $servicesbaseline $servicesnow


And the lab finds:

Dynamics    =>


Remember our arrow rule?

=>

Current/difference side

So:

Dynamics exists in the machine's current service list but wasn't in the baseline.

That makes Dynamics a new service worth investigating.

It doesn't alone prove the service is malicious.

